Privacy Policy for BlockApps
Last Updated: October 26, 2023
Welcome to BlockApps, developed by Pankaj Sejwal. Your privacy is our top priority. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle your information when you use our application.
1. No Data Collection or Transmission
BlockApps is a local-only utility. We do not collect, store, or transmit any personal data, usage statistics, or device information to external servers. All processing related to app blocking and scheduling happens strictly on your device.
2. Sensitive Permissions & How We Use Them
To provide its core functionality, BlockApps requires specific sensitive permissions. We use these only for the purposes described below:
•
Usage Access (PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS): This permission is required to detect which application is currently in the foreground. This allows BlockApps to determine if an app is on your "Blocked List" or has exceeded a "Scheduled Limit" so it can trigger the lock screen.
•
Overlay Permission (SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW): This allows BlockApps to display a secure lock screen over blocked applications. Without this, the app cannot prevent access to restricted content.
•
Query All Packages: We use this to generate the list of installed applications on your device, allowing you to select which ones you wish to protect or schedule.
•
Biometric Data: BlockApps uses the standard Android Biometric API to allow you to unlock apps. We do not have access to your actual biometric data (fingerprints or face scans); the verification is handled entirely by the Android System.
3. Third-Party Sharing
We do not sell, trade, or share any information with third parties. Since no data is collected or transmitted, there is no data available to be shared.
4. Data Security
Your App Lock PIN and schedules are stored locally in your device's private storage. These are not accessible to other applications and are cleared if you uninstall the app.
5. Children’s Privacy
BlockApps does not collect any personal information from children. Our app is intended to help users manage their own productivity and screen time.
6. Changes to This Policy
We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page and updating the "Last Updated" date.
7. Contact Us
If you have any questions or suggestions about our Privacy Policy, do not hesitate to contact us.
